    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1087">

                <pb facs="0809" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1402</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker, representing American interests, to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-22T14:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1916, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>415. Department’s 423, September 18, 6 p.m. Decree dated June 19, 1915, provides:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Taxes paid to pretended authorities before occupation by
                            Constitutionalist forces are considered paid. Rear taxes should be paid
                            within a month from occupation thereafter with penalties. If taxes
                            should have been paid in advance they must be repaid.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Nevertheless I am making investigation for a more recent decree relating
                    thereto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
